# The only root-context build is the MCP image: apps/mcp/Cargo.toml
# path-depends on ../../crates/fluxvale-api, so its context must span
# both trees, and Docker can't COPY above a context. Every other image
# (apps/platform) builds from its own subdirectory context, which
# ignores this file entirely.
#
# Deny-by-default — only what apps/mcp/Dockerfile COPYs rides the
# context (the #15 lesson: an unscoped root context ships everything,
# node_modules included). Local build artifacts stay out (**/target).
*
!apps
!crates
apps/*
crates/*
!apps/mcp
!crates/fluxvale-api
!crates/Cargo.toml
**/target
